      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks unsafe, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. That's about twice the labeled maximum of **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release metformin, and the extended-release maximum is lower, at 2000 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What may have been intended:**\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). 1700 is exactly 2 \u00d7 850, so this mix-up seems likely.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **1000 mg twice daily**, or another regimen you specify.\n\nPlease let me know the correct dose and frequency, and whether it's immediate- or extended-release. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll put it in the order note for pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
